Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  

• countries.country_name / countries.country_id : identify “France” and get its country_id to link to customers.  
• customers.country_id / customers.cust_id   : locate all French customers and join to sales.  
• sales.cust_id / sales.prod_id / sales.time_id / sales.channel_id / sales.promo_id / sales.amount_sold  
                       : base fact table – we need the amount sold per product, month and year.  
• promotions.promo_id / promotions.promo_total_id : keep only rows where promo_total_id = 1.  
• channels.channel_id / channels.channel_total_id : keep only rows where channel_total_id = 1.  
• times.time_id / times.calendar_year / times.calendar_month_number : turn each sale‑date into year & month (2019, 2020, 2021).  
• currency.country / currency.year / currency.month / currency.to_us : 2021 exchange rate to convert projected sales into USD.  
• sales.quantity_sold (optional)         : not required here, focus on amount_sold.  

Main filtering conditions that will repeatedly appear  
 1. countries.country_name = 'France'  
 2. promotions.promo_total_id = 1  
 3. channels.channel_total_id  = 1  
 4. times.calendar_year IN (2019, 2020, 2021)  

Below are ten exploratory SQL queries (each capped with LIMIT 20 rows and using DISTINCT where possible) that gradually build up the information needed for the final calculation.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Find the row that represents France and capture its country_id.
SELECT DISTINCT country_id, country_name
FROM countries
WHERE country_name LIKE '%France%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: List a few customer IDs that belong to France.
SELECT DISTINCT cust_id
FROM customers
WHERE country_id = (
        SELECT country_id 
        FROM countries
        WHERE country_name = 'France'
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Verify which promotions have promo_total_id = 1.
SELECT DISTINCT promo_id, promo_name
FROM promotions
WHERE promo_total_id = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Verify which channels have channel_total_id = 1.
SELECT DISTINCT channel_id, channel_desc
FROM channels
WHERE channel_total_id = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Show a sample of raw sales rows in 2019 that satisfy ALL filters (France, promo_total_id=1, channel_total_id=1).
SELECT DISTINCT s.prod_id, s.cust_id, s.time_id, s.amount_sold
FROM sales        AS s
JOIN customers    AS c  ON s.cust_id   = c.cust_id
JOIN countries    AS co ON c.country_id = co.country_id
JOIN promotions   AS p  ON s.promo_id  = p.promo_id
JOIN channels     AS ch ON s.channel_id = ch.channel_id
WHERE co.country_name = 'France'
  AND p.promo_total_id = 1
  AND ch.channel_total_id = 1
  AND s.time_id BETWEEN '2019-01-01' AND '2019-12-31'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Aggregate monthly 2019 sales (per product) that meet the same filters.
SELECT t.calendar_month_number  AS month,
       s.prod_id,
       SUM(s.amount_sold)       AS total_2019
FROM  sales      AS s
JOIN  customers  AS c   ON s.cust_id   = c.cust_id
JOIN  countries  AS co  ON c.country_id = co.country_id
JOIN  promotions AS p   ON s.promo_id  = p.promo_id
JOIN  channels   AS ch  ON s.channel_id = ch.channel_id
JOIN  times      AS t   ON s.time_id   = t.time_id
WHERE co.country_name   = 'France'
  AND p.promo_total_id  = 1
  AND ch.channel_total_id = 1
  AND t.calendar_year    = 2019
GROUP BY t.calendar_month_number, s.prod_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Aggregate monthly 2020 sales (per product) with the same filters.
SELECT t.calendar_month_number  AS month,
       s.prod_id,
       SUM(s.amount_sold)       AS total_2020
FROM  sales      AS s
JOIN  customers  AS c   ON s.cust_id   = c.cust_id
JOIN  countries  AS co  ON c.country_id = co.country_id
JOIN  promotions AS p   ON s.promo_id  = p.promo_id
JOIN  channels   AS ch  ON s.channel_id = ch.channel_id
JOIN  times      AS t   ON s.time_id   = t.time_id
WHERE co.country_name   = 'France'
  AND p.promo_total_id  = 1
  AND ch.channel_total_id = 1
  AND t.calendar_year    = 2020
GROUP BY t.calendar_month_number, s.prod_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Compute the 2019→2020 growth rate for each product & month.
SELECT a.prod_id,
       a.month,
       (b.total_2020 - a.total_2019) * 1.0 / NULLIF(a.total_2019, 0)  AS growth_rate
FROM (
        /* 2019 totals (built from query #6) */
        SELECT t.calendar_month_number AS month,
               s.prod_id,
               SUM(s.amount_sold) AS total_2019
        FROM sales s
        JOIN customers c   ON s.cust_id   = c.cust_id
        JOIN countries co  ON c.country_id = co.country_id
        JOIN promotions p  ON s.promo_id  = p.promo_id
        JOIN channels  ch  ON s.channel_id = ch.channel_id
        JOIN times     t   ON s.time_id   = t.time_id
        WHERE co.country_name = 'France'
          AND p.promo_total_id = 1
          AND ch.channel_total_id = 1
          AND t.calendar_year = 2019
        GROUP BY t.calendar_month_number, s.prod_id
     ) a
JOIN (
        /* 2020 totals (built from query #7) */
        SELECT t.calendar_month_number AS month,
               s.prod_id,
               SUM(s.amount_sold) AS total_2020
        FROM sales s
        JOIN customers c   ON s.cust_id   = c.cust_id
        JOIN countries co  ON c.country_id = co.country_id
        JOIN promotions p  ON s.promo_id  = p.promo_id
        JOIN channels  ch  ON s.channel_id = ch.channel_id
        JOIN times     t   ON s.time_id   = t.time_id
        WHERE co.country_name = 'France'
          AND p.promo_total_id = 1
          AND ch.channel_total_id = 1
          AND t.calendar_year = 2020
        GROUP BY t.calendar_month_number, s.prod_id
     ) b
  ON a.prod_id = b.prod_id AND a.month = b.month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Project 2021 sales per product & month by applying the growth rate to 2020 totals.
SELECT b.prod_id,
       b.month,
       b.total_2020 * (1 + g.growth_rate)                 AS projected_2021
FROM (
        /* 2020 totals again */
        SELECT t.calendar_month_number AS month,
               s.prod_id,
               SUM(s.amount_sold) AS total_2020
        FROM sales s
        JOIN customers c   ON s.cust_id   = c.cust_id
        JOIN countries co  ON c.country_id = co.country_id
        JOIN promotions p  ON s.promo_id  = p.promo_id
        JOIN channels  ch  ON s.channel_id = ch.channel_id
        JOIN times     t   ON s.time_id   = t.time_id
        WHERE co.country_name = 'France'
          AND p.promo_total_id = 1
          AND ch.channel_total_id = 1
          AND t.calendar_year = 2020
        GROUP BY t.calendar_month_number, s.prod_id
     ) b
JOIN (
        /* growth rate from query #8, aliased as g */
        SELECT prod_id, month, 
               (total_2020 - total_2019) * 1.0 / NULLIF(total_2019,0) AS growth_rate
        FROM (
              /* embed 2019 vs 2020 pairs again */
              SELECT a.prod_id, a.month, a.total_2019, c.total_2020
              FROM (
                    SELECT t.calendar_month_number AS month,
                           s.prod_id,
                           SUM(s.amount_sold) AS total_2019
                    FROM sales s
                    JOIN customers c ON s.cust_id = c.cust_id
                    JOIN countries co ON c.country_id = co.country_id
                    JOIN promotions p ON s.promo_id = p.promo_id
                    JOIN channels ch ON s.channel_id = ch.channel_id
                    JOIN times t ON s.time_id = t.time_id
                    WHERE co.country_name = 'France'
                      AND p.promo_total_id = 1
                      AND ch.channel_total_id = 1
                      AND t.calendar_year = 2019
                    GROUP BY t.calendar_month_number, s.prod_id
                   ) a
              JOIN (
                    SELECT t.calendar_month_number AS month,
                           s.prod_id,
                           SUM(s.amount_sold) AS total_2020
                    FROM sales s
                    JOIN customers c ON s.cust_id = c.cust_id
                    JOIN countries co ON c.country_id = co.country_id
                    JOIN promotions p ON s.promo_id = p.promo_id
                    JOIN channels ch ON s.channel_id = ch.channel_id
                    JOIN times t ON s.time_id = t.time_id
                    WHERE co.country_name = 'France'
                      AND p.promo_total_id = 1
                      AND ch.channel_total_id = 1
                      AND t.calendar_year = 2020
                    GROUP BY t.calendar_month_number, s.prod_id
                   ) c
                ON a.prod_id = c.prod_id AND a.month = c.month
             )
     ) g
  ON g.prod_id = b.prod_id AND g.month = b.month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Convert the projected 2021 sales into USD and average them by month.
SELECT proj.month,
       AVG(proj.projected_2021 / cu.to_us)   AS avg_projected_2021_usd
FROM (
        /* projected numbers from query #9 */
        SELECT b.prod_id,
               b.month,
               b.total_2020 * (1 + g.growth_rate) AS projected_2021
        FROM ...  -- same sub‑query block as in #9 (omitted here for brevity)
     )  AS proj
JOIN currency AS cu
     ON cu.country = 'France'
    AND cu.year    = 2021
    AND cu.month   = proj.month
GROUP BY proj.month
ORDER BY proj.month
LIMIT 20;
```

These ten queries step through the whole problem—from identifying France, confirming valid promotion & channel rows, inspecting the raw sales, gathering monthly totals for 2019 and 2020, deriving per‑product growth, projecting 2021 sales, converting to USD with 2021 exchange rates, and finally averaging the projections by month.
